        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the idea!\r\n\r\nAt the moment I don't think this introduces *that* different approach from the current one. How I currently assume things should work:\r\n- User installs 'mini.ai' and 'notebook-navigator'.\r\n- Has the following setup for 'mini.ai':\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\r\n  custom_textobjects = {\r\n    h = require('notebook-naviagtor').notebook_navigator_textobject\r\n  }\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nOn a side note, I'd suggest using \"textobject specification\" or just \"specification\" instead of plain \"textobject\". Maybe something like `require('notebook-naviagtor').miniai_spec`?",
