        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for responding so quickly.\r\n\r\nI thought about the approach you are proposing above but chose not to go that way because it would mean that now the mini.ai configuration depends on a plugin from some random person. This is particularly noticeable when you are specifying   package dependencies upfront (as you do in packer or lazy). Now for each textobject specification I want to bring from outside, my mini.ai config adds one dependency and to me at least that feels a bit off.\r\n\r\nLet me know if you change your mind on the topic and thanks again for all the amazing plugins.\r\n\r\nP.S. I'm taking your advice above on naming conventions",
