        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I thought about the approach you are proposing above but chose not to go that way because it would mean that now the mini.ai configuration depends on a plugin from some random person. This is particularly noticeable when you are specifying package dependencies upfront (as you do in packer or lazy). Now for each textobject specification I want to bring from outside, my mini.ai config adds one dependency and to me at least that feels a bit off.\r\n\r\nThe alternative would be to specify 'mini.ai' as dependency for *every* plugin implementing textobject specification for 'mini.ai', which to me feels a bit off.\r\n\r\nHaving \"external\" plugins as dependency in one place (for 'mini.ai') seems more straightforward as it enables explicit configuration of `a`/`i` textobjects one place. Similar to relation of 'nvim-cmp' and its sources.",
