        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> The alternative would be to specify 'mini.ai' as dependency for every plugin implementing textobject specification for 'mini.ai', which to me feels a bit off.\r\n\r\nAnd to me feels more natural :D. I'm coming from the perspective of using 'mini.ai' as a sort of library while your point of view seems (to me) to be that 'mini.ai' is more an application that takes on dependencies. I'm afraid I don't have any particularly strong argument here so I will let it be, and then of course, your house your rules.\r\n\r\nThanks for entertaining me and please do let me know if you'd like somebody to work on such a feature.",
